# Known MODERATE/HIGH/CRITICAL npm advisories in integrations/solana-agent-kit/package-lock.json (the SAK adapter).
# Read by gate.mjs in the CI supply-chain job. One `GHSA-id@package` per line
# (the advisory in that package only); the rest of the line is a note. A new
# advisory at moderate or above fails CI (moderate since 2026-10-20); so does
# a listed one that is no longer reported (prune it in the change that fixes it).
#
# Recorded 2026-09-30. At 3327fcf this tree carried 36 distinct high/critical
# advisories (3 critical). 35 are gone:
#   - The bridge no longer loads @solana-agent-kit/plugin-defi or plugin-token
#     (it never called them; importing one ran its whole dependency tree in
#     the process holding the private key). That removed the Drift, OKX,
#     Meteora, Orca, Pyth and Switchboard trees: 25 advisories, all three
#     criticals.
#   - package.json `overrides` force patched versions inside the same major
#     line where the parent had not moved: fast-uri 3.1.8, nanoid 3.3.19,
#     jsondiffpatch 0.7.6, langsmith 0.6.3, hono 4.13.12, ip-address 10.7.2,
#     qs 6.16.0. Typecheck and all bridge tests pass on them.
#
# What remains has no fix that can be applied from here:
GHSA-3gc7-fjrx-p6mg@bigint-buffer  # high  bigint-buffer <=1.1.5 (no patched release exists): solana-agent-kit 2.0.10 -> @solana/spl-token 0.4.15 -> @solana/buffer-layout-utils 0.3.0 -> bigint-buffer 1.1.5 (npm ls, 2026-10-02). The overflow is in the package's NATIVE addon (toBigIntLE). Every install of this tree runs with --ignore-scripts, so the addon is never built and bigint-buffer runs its pure-JS fallback. Since R-P8 phase 3 (2026-10-02) only this adapter package depends on solana-agent-kit: the guard that signs (integrations/agent-guard) and every other integration do not carry this advisory.
#
# Moderate, listed since the gate began to fail on moderate (2026-10-20). The
# four come through jayson 4.3.0, web3.js 1.x's HTTP JSON-RPC client; web3.js
# loads only `jayson/lib/client/browser`, which requires `uuid` (v4) and
# nothing that loads stream-json. npm's only offered fix is web3.js 3.x.
GHSA-528h-pc64-c93x@stream-json  # moderate  stream-json <=3.4.0: O(depth^2) filters (DoS). Required only by jayson/lib/utils.js (server-side stream parsing), never by the client web3.js loads.
GHSA-hqr4-qq8f-hg3x@stream-json  # moderate  stream-json <=3.5.0: JSONC comment re-scan per chunk (DoS). Same path: never loaded.
GHSA-mjw6-4jj6-33hc@stream-json  # moderate  stream-json <3.6.0: prototype pollution in Assembler. Same path: no RPC answer reaches it.
GHSA-w5hq-g745-h8pq@uuid  # moderate  uuid <11.1.1: bounds check missing in v3/v5/v6 with a caller-supplied buffer. jayson calls v4() and @langchain/core calls v4/v5 without a buffer. Forcing uuid across three majors into web3.js was judged riskier than the advisory.
#
# Not listed, and failing the gate until fixed (2026-10-20): @modelcontextprotocol/sdk
# <1.32.0 carries GHSA-22jm-h49p-29qw (high) and GHSA-6prh-2h8m-c8cw
# (moderate), both with a fix npm marks non-breaking. The remedy is an
# `overrides` entry forcing @modelcontextprotocol/sdk >=1.32.0 in
# integrations/solana-agent-kit/package.json, not an entry here.
#
# Below the gate's threshold (low), recorded for completeness:
#   - ai <5.0.52 (GHSA-rwvc-j5jr-mgvh) and @ai-sdk/provider-utils <3.0.28
#     (GHSA-866g-f22w-33x8): fixed only in the ai 5 line, which
#     solana-agent-kit 2.x does not use.
